   "reference": {
    "title": "WHO 5th urethral & periurethral carcinoma — dual-track AJCC 8th staging",
    "intro": "Urethral carcinomas follow two separate AJCC 8th pT tables depending on anatomic site: Male penile/bulbomembranous & female urethra vs Prostatic urethra. Specify percentages of any urothelial histologic subtypes or divergent differentiations.",
    "note": "Photomicrographs are from Wikimedia Commons under open Creative Commons licences. ExpertPath pages open with your own ExpertPath login; the app holds none of their images.",
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "Site-specific tumour spectrum & staging landmarks",
      "points": [
       "Distal male/female urethra predominantly yields squamous cell carcinoma; proximal/prostatic urethra yields urothelial carcinoma; urethral diverticula (especially in females) are enriched for clear cell adenocarcinoma (PAX8+, HNF1beta+, Napsin A+) and enteric/mucinous adenocarcinoma.",
       "Prostatic urethra pT: pTis = CIS involving prostatic urethra or prostatic ducts without stromal invasion; pT1 = subepithelial connective tissue; pT2 = prostatic stroma; pT3 = periprostatic fat; pT4 = extraprostatic bladder wall / rectal wall / seminal vesicle.",
       "Male penile / female urethra pT: pT2 = corpus spongiosum or periurethral muscle; pT3 = corpus cavernosum or anterior vagina; pT4 = bladder wall or other adjacent organs."
      ],
